# Documentation governance

> If it is not documented, it does not exist.

## Impact classification

| Impact | When | Required updates |
| ------ | ---- | ---------------- |
| **NONE** | Comment-only, internal refactor with no behavior change | None |
| **LOW** | New test, locator tweak, minor helper | `specs/test.plan.md` if scenario changes |
| **MEDIUM** | New feature module, new test layer, CI change | README + architecture or test plan |
| **HIGH** | Layer rule change, credential policy, major restructure | ADR + `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` + README |

When unclear, default to **MEDIUM**.

## Document map (this project only)

| Document | Update when |
| -------- | ----------- |
| [README.md](../README.md) | Commands, env vars, user-facing behavior, structure |
| [docs/ARCHITECTURE.md](../docs/ARCHITECTURE.md) | Features, layers, diagrams, import rules |
| [docs/adr/*.md](../docs/adr/) | Non-trivial design decisions |
| [specs/test.plan.md](../specs/test.plan.md) | New/changed test scenarios |
| [specs/README.md](../specs/README.md) | Specs folder purpose changes |
| [.env.example](../.env.example) | New or changed environment variables |

**Do not reference** AI-Investor paths (`docs/architecture/AI-INVESTOR-*`, `docs/roadmap/`, etc.) — they do not exist in this repo.

## ADR required when

- New feature module or layer boundary change
- CI/credential policy change
- HTTP client or test strategy pattern change
- Breaking change to `pw-core` public API

## Quality bar

- Terminology matches [docs/ARCHITECTURE.md](../docs/ARCHITECTURE.md)
- README reflects actual commands and paths
- Mermaid diagrams updated when structure changes
